---@meta
-- Generated by rs3-api-types from https://developer.runescape.com/rs/ui/decorative_components/radial_progress_overlay.html;
-- regenerate it with ./gradlew generate rather than editing it.

---These components are a performant way to represent progression via an indicator that pans across radially as it
---advances. They support both automatic, time-based progression, and manual progression, making them ideal for elements
---like ability cooldown timers and skill experience trackers for example.
---@class ui.RadialProgressOverlay : ui.Component
---@field curValue number The current value for this overlay, ranging between `initialValue` and `endValue`. This can be set, allowing the creation of progress indicators that don't start at `initialValue`.
---@field initialValue number (Read-only) The initial value for this overlay, as specified via `Set`.
---@field endValue number (Read-only) The final value for this overlay, as specified via `Set`.
---@field progress number (Read-only) The current progress percentage for this overlay, ranging from `0` to `1`, representing `0%` and `100%` respectively.
---@field maskSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the overlay's visuals, normally used as a transparency mask.
ui.RadialProgressOverlay = {}

---Creates a new radial progress overlay on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this radial progress overlay in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.RadialProgressOverlay # The newly created radial progress overlay. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.RadialProgressOverlay.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Sets the value range for this component and any additional flags to modify its behaviour.
---
---Info: To have the overlay behave as a timer, pass `ui.RadialProgressOverlayFlag.AUTOMATIC` as part of the flags. Note
---when using this flag, `initialValue` and `endValue` represent time in seconds.
---@param initialValue number The starting value for this overlay.
---@param endValue number The final value for this overlay.
---@param flags integer Combination of flags used to determine how this radial is displayed and whether or not it should automatically progress after this function call.
function ui.RadialProgressOverlay:Start(initialValue, endValue, flags) end

---Enumeration containing flags used to control RadialProgressOverlay behaviour and visuals.
---@enum ui.RadialProgressOverlayFlag
ui.RadialProgressOverlayFlag = {
    ---Indicates that once started, this overlay's progress will automatically advance over time. This is ideal for timer overlays.
    AUTOMATIC = 1,
    ---Indicates the overlay starts filled and gradually depletes.
    REVERSE = 2,
    ---Inverts the overlay's visuals horizontally.
    FLIP_HORIZONTAL = 4,
    ---Inverts the overlay's visuals vertical.
    FLIP_VERTICAL = 8,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `ui.RadialProgressOverlayFlag.FromID(ui.RadialProgressOverlayFlag.AUTOMATIC)` is `"AUTOMATIC"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function ui.RadialProgressOverlayFlag.FromID(value) end
